  "description": "<p>After a Fedora relase, fcrepo4-vagrant is then tied to the SNAPSHOT version. However those artifacts are generally not recreated during the development cycle. Therefore there is no difference between the release and the post-release artifacts.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore it makes sense that fcrepo4-vagrant should only be updated at a release of Fedora and left there until the next release.</p>\n\n<p>Tagging <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Afe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:fe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" data-account-id=\"557058:fe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" accountid=\"557058:fe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Nick Ruest</a> for thoughts?</p>",
